  "title": "Taharqa",
  "summary": "Taharqa, who came from Napata in Kush, ruled Egypt as a pharaoh of the Twenty-fifth Dynasty from 690 to 664 BCE. He tried to reunite Egypt and Nubia against Assyria and built many temples, but Assyrian forces sacked Memphis and drove him back south. He was buried in a large pyramid at Nuri.",
